 This document outlines best practices for setting up and testing webhooks in ElizaOS projects, particularly when using ngrok for local development. Following these guidelines will help prevent common issues and provide a reliable testing workflow.

## Ngrok URL Detection

### Domain Pattern Awareness

- Ngrok uses different domain patterns based on account type:
  - Free accounts: `*.ngrok-free.app`
  - Paid accounts: `*.ngrok.app`
  - Both formats should be supported in scripts

### Robust URL Extraction

Always use a domain-agnostic approach to extract ngrok URLs from API responses:

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT: Extract URL from JSON response
TUNNELS_JSON=$(curl -s http://127.0.0.1:4040/api/tunnels)
NGROK_URL=$(echo "$TUNNELS_JSON" | grep -o '"public_url":"https://[^"]*"' | sed 's/"public_url":"//g' | sed 's/"//g' | head -n 1)

# ❌ INCORRECT: Hardcoding specific domain patterns
NGROK_URL=$(curl -s http://127.0.0.1:4040/api/tunnels | grep -o "https://[^\"]*\.ngrok-free.app")
```

In TypeScript:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT: Extract URL from tunnel object
const tunnelsResponse = await axios.get('http://localhost:4040/api/tunnels');
const tunnels = tunnelsResponse.data.tunnels || [];
const httpsTunnel = tunnels.find((t: any) => t.proto === 'https');
if (httpsTunnel) {
  ngrokUrl = httpsTunnel.public_url;
}

// ❌ INCORRECT: Using regex with specific domain patterns
const tunnelsText = await axios.get('http://localhost:4040/api/tunnels');
const match = tunnelsText.match(/https:\/\/[^"]*\.ngrok-free\.app/);
if (match) {
  ngrokUrl = match[0];
}
```

## Webhook Testing Architecture

### Test Endpoints for Development

Create separate test endpoints that bypass signature verification for local development:

```typescript
// In your Express router:
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
  router.post('/api/test/webhooks/:provider', async (req, res) => {
    // Bypass signature verification for testing
    try {
      await handleWebhookEvent(req.body);
      return res.status(200).json({ success: true, message: "Test webhook received" });
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error handling test webhook:', error);
      return res.status(500).json({ success: false, error: error.message });
    }
  });
}
```

